    "0energies are negative because the\n"
    "0electron is bound.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Photon from a transition\n"
    "2E_photon = E_high - E_low\n"
    "2hf = E_i - E_f\n"
    "0Absorption lifts an electron up;\n"
    "0emission drops it down and releases a\n"
    "0photon.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Why spectra are line spectra\n"
    "0Only certain energies are allowed, so\n"
    "0only certain photon energies appear.\n"
    "0Each element has its own fingerprint,\n"
    "0which is how the composition of stars\n"
    "0is known.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Ionisation energy of hydrogen\n"
    "213.6 eV, from n = 1 to n = infinity\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Emission vs absorption\n"
    "0A hot thin gas emits bright lines. A\n"
    "0cool gas in front of a continuous\n"
    "0source absorbs the very same lines,\n"
    "0leaving dark gaps.";

static const char body_12_3[] =
    "1Notation\n"
    "2A = mass number (protons + neutrons)\n"
    "2Z = atomic number (protons)\n"
    "2N = A - Z (neutrons)\n"
    "0Isotopes share Z and differ in N.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Mass defect and binding energy\n"
    "0The nucleus weighs less than its\n"
    "0parts.\n"
    "2E = m*c^2\n"
    "21 u = 931.5 MeV/c^2\n"
    "0The missing mass is the binding\n"
    "0energy that holds it together.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Binding energy per nucleon\n"
    "0Peaks near iron-56. That is why\n"
    "0fusing light nuclei releases energy,\n"
    "0and so does splitting heavy ones.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Fission\n"
    "0A heavy nucleus splits, releasing\n"
    "0energy and more neutrons, which can\n"
    "0sustain a chain reaction. This is a\n"
    "0nuclear reactor or a fission bomb.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Fusion\n"
    "0Light nuclei merge. This powers the\n"
    "0Sun, which fuses hydrogen into\n"
    "0helium, and it releases more energy\n"
    "0per kilogram than fission.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1The strong force\n"
    "0Binds nucleons but has an extremely\n"
    "0short range, so very large nuclei are\n"
    "0unstable.";

static const char body_12_4[] =
    "1Alpha decay\n"
    "0Emits a helium nucleus.\n"
    "2A decreases by 4, Z by 2\n"
    "0Stopped by paper or skin.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Beta minus decay\n"
    "0A neutron becomes a proton and an\n"
    "0electron.\n"
    "2A unchanged, Z increases by 1\n"
    "0Stopped by a few millimetres of\n"
    "0aluminium.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Beta plus decay\n"
    "0A proton becomes a neutron and a\n"
    "0positron.\n"
    "2A unchanged, Z decreases by 1\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Gamma decay\n"
    "0A photon from a nucleus dropping to a\n"
    "0lower state.\n"
    "2A and Z unchanged\n"
    "0Needs thick lead or concrete.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Half life\n"
    "2N = N0 * (1/2)^(t/T_half)\n"
    "2A = A0 * (1/2)^(t/T_half)\n"
    "0After n half lives, the fraction left\n"
    "0is (1/2)^n.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Decay constant\n"
    "2N = N0 * e^(-lambda*t)\n"
    "2T_half = ln(2)/lambda = 0.693/lambda\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Carbon dating\n"
    "0Living things hold a steady ratio of\n"
    "0carbon-14; once dead it decays with a\n"
    "0half life of 5730 years, giving the\n"
    "0age.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Conservation rules\n"
    "0A and Z each balance across a nuclear\n"
    "0equation. Use that to identify the\n"
    "0missing particle.";

static const char body_12_5[] =
    "1The two postulates\n"
    "01. The laws of physics are the same\n"
    "0in every inertial frame. 2. The speed\n"
    "0of light in vacuum is the same for\n"
    "0every observer, whatever their\n"
    "0motion.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Lorentz factor\n"
    "2gamma = 1/sqrt(1 - v^2/c^2)\n"
    "0gamma is 1 at rest and grows without\n"
    "0limit as v approaches c.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Time dilation\n"
    "2t = gamma * t_proper\n"
    "0Moving clocks run slow. Proper time\n"
    "0is measured in the frame where the\n"
    "0two events happen at the same place.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Length contraction\n"
    "2L = L_proper/gamma\n"
    "0Lengths shrink along the direction of\n"
    "0motion only.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Evidence\n"
    "0Muons created high in the atmosphere\n"
    "0reach the ground even though they\n"
    "0should decay first. In our frame\n"
    "0their clocks run slow; in theirs the\n"
    "0atmosphere is contracted.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Relativistic energy\n"
    "2E = gamma*m*c^2\n"
    "2E_rest = m*c^2\n"
    "2KE = (gamma - 1)*m*c^2\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Why c is a limit\n"
    "0Accelerating a mass to c would take\n"
    "0infinite energy, so only massless\n"
    "0particles travel at c.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1When it matters\n"
    "0At v = 0.1c gamma is only 1.005.\n"
    "0Below about 10% of c the classical\n"
    "0formulas are fine.";

