static const char body_13_5[] =
    "1A reliable order\n"
    "01. Draw a picture, label the knowns.\n"
    "02. Choose a system and a sign\n"
    "0convention. 3. Name the physics: is\n"
    "0it kinematics, forces, energy, or\n"
    "0momentum? 4. Write the equation\n"
    "0symbolically. 5. Solve for the\n"
    "0unknown BEFORE putting numbers in. 6.\n"
    "0Substitute with units. 7. Check the\n"
    "0size, the sign and the units.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Choosing the tool\n"
    "2time or acceleration involved: forces\n"
    "2and kinematics\n"
    "2speed and height, no time: energy\n"
    "2a collision or explosion: momentum\n"
    "2rotation: torque and angular momentum\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Sanity checks\n"
    "3Does the answer have the right\n"
    "3\001units?\n"
    "3Is the sign meaningful?\n"
    "3Is the size plausible? A car does\n"
    "3\001not weigh 3 N and a person does not\n"
    "3\001run at 100 m/s.\n"
    "3Do the limiting cases behave? Set\n"
    "3\001an angle to 0 or 90 degrees and see\n"
    "3\001whether the formula still makes\n"
    "3\001sense.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Common errors\n"
    "3Degrees vs radians in the wrong\n"
    "3\001MODE.\n"
    "3Forgetting that g is downward.\n"
    "3Using kinematic equations when the\n"
    "3\001acceleration is not constant.\n"
    "3Adding vector magnitudes directly.\n"
    "3Leaving temperatures in Celsius in\n"
    "3\001a gas law.";

